        'description' => 'The VASWCD Educational Foundation Inc. Scholarship Awards Program is a fantastic opportunity for Virginia residents who are high school seniors or college freshmen passionate about natural resource conservation and environmental protection. This program provides financial support to students who are currently or planning to major in a course curriculum related to these fields. To be eligible, applicants must have a class ranking in the top 20% of their graduating class or a 3.0 or greater GPA. If you\'re interested in applying, contact your local SWCD or the Association office for an application specific to your Soil & Water Conservation District. If you\'re eligible, we encourage you to apply. Don\'t miss out on this chance to pursue your dreams and make a difference in the world of environmental health! P.S.: Scholarship deadlines vary slightly by district. To find the exact scholarship deadline for your district, find your Local Soil & Water Conservation District here and contact them.',
