        'description' => 'Are you an incoming Sam Houston State "Bearkat" from Texas? If so, you may be in luck! The Smith-Hutson Freshman Scholarship was established to financially support Texas high school graduates who will be attending Sam Houston State University in the upcoming academic year. Incoming Bearkats must also demonstrate financial need, academic achievement, and leadership potential to qualify. The scholarship is a "completer" scholarship, meaning that recipients may earn a maximum of $20,000, after accounting for other scholarship awards received. Thus, if recipients were to earn $5,000 from another scholarship, the Smith-Hutson Freshman Scholarship would grant the remaining $15,000. The scholarship may be renewed for a maximum of eight (8) semesters so long as recipients maintain a cumulative GPA of 2.5 and a minimum of 30 semester credit hours each year. If this sounds like a good opportunity for you, we encourage you to apply! Then, be sure to check out these other Texas scholarships available on Scholarships360. Good luck with your scholarship search!',
