        'description' => 'Don and Dorothy Cummins were a passionate couple, both heavily involved in their community and dedicated to making it a better place. While Dorothy served as a secretary to the president of Northeastern Junior College, on top of being a Cub and Girl Scout Leader and a member of her church choir, Don was heavily involved in various philanthropic activities. The couple lived in Fort Lupton, Colorado, in 1959, and would go on to live there for the next five decades. In their honor, the Cummins Care Scholarship annually awards $2,000 each to multiple Fort Lupton High School seniors and GED students each year! In addition to graduating from Fort Lupton High School, applicants must be planning to attend any accredited two- or four-year college, university, or vocational school in the United States. They should also demonstrate financial need. Finalists should bear in mind that participation in the FLHS Meet the Scholars Night will be included in scholarship application scoring and evaluation. Looking for similar scholarships you may be eligible for? Consider checking out our other Colorado scholarships! Apply today to take the first steps toward your future.',
