        'description' => 'Consistently rated as one of the most beautiful cities across the United States, Chicago is also known for its amazing food scene and large, 2.7-million population. To account for such a large resident pool, Chicago Public Schools itself consists of 148 high schools. If you are lucky enough to attend one of these schools in the "Windy City," the Wentcher Foundation may have just the scholarship opportunity for you! Each year, their Wentcher Foundation Scholarship - Chicago Public Schools awards up to $10,000 each a year to multiple high school seniors at any Chicago Public High School. Applicants must also hold a minimum 3.0 GPA and should demonstrate high character and leadership at home, at school, or in their communities. The scholarship may be renewed for four years of undergraduate schooling. If you sound like a fit for this scholarship, we encourage you to apply! Plus, don’t forget to explore Scholarships360 for similar scholarships! There are plenty of other scholarships for Illinois residents and community service scholarships available through our platform. Happy applying!',
