        'description' => 'Paul Yeager was a multitalented individual, balancing work at the physical science department of Diablo Valley College and his hobbies of bicycling, backpacking, skiing, and hiking. He was also a devoted friend, meticulously organizing large group trips to spend time with each other. To support those who share Paul\'s love for the physical sciences, the Community Foundation San Luis Obispo County is offering a $23,000 scholarship! To qualify for the scholarship, individuals must be college-bound high school seniors at Coast Union, Morro Bay, or Paso Robles High School. Applicants must also have a minimum 2.5 GPA and plan to pursue a degree in physical science or technical areas at a California Community College and/or a California State University or University of California system school. The scholarship will be distributed as follows: $3,000 toward freshman year, $5,000 toward sophomore year, $7,000 toward junior year, and 8,000 toward the recipient\'s senior year of college. If you sound like a fit for this scholarship, we encourage you to also explore other California scholarships and physical science scholarships available through Scholarships360. Good luck with your scholarship search!',
