        'description' => 'Are you interested in joining your university\'s honor program? Well, if you\'re an incoming Manhattanville University student or current underclassman, you\'re in luck! The Castle Scholars Honors Program is a wonderful opportunity offering both the chance to partake in a college Honors Program and earn an annual $2,000 - $3,000 scholarship (upon maintenance of renewal criteria). Admission to the program is typically limited to incoming first-year students, but students can apply up until the second semester of their sophomore year. While first-year students with a high school GPA of 3.9 or higher will automatically be invited to apply for the program, current Manhattanville students must have a minimum 3.7 GPA and submit a written recommendation from their academic advisor. Students in the honors program will receive special privileges, such as priority class registration, access to reserved study areas, special social events and field trips, mentoring from Honors Program faculty, and more. The scholarship will be renewed each year upon maintenance of Castle Scholars Honors Program criteria. If this sounds like a good opportunity for you, we encourage you to apply!',
