        'description' => 'There are many benefits to living in rural areas, including a lower cost of living, a stronger sense of community, and better air quality. However, individuals from these areas are often overlooked when it comes to college recruitment, and students from rural areas have lower rates of college enrollment than their urban and suburban peers as a result. To provide support and encouragement to students living in rural areas, the Texas Rural Education Association is offering the Dr. Max Thompson Honorary Scholarship! This scholarship, worth $2,000, is open to high school seniors in school districts that belong to the Texas Rural Education Association (TREA). Applicants must also be planning to enroll in a post-graduate program, attend a technical school, or enlist in the military the following school year. The Dr. Max Thompson Honorary Scholarship is just one of the many scholarships for Texas residents available on Scholarships360. If it sounds like a good opportunity for you, we encourage you to apply and explore others you may qualify for as well. Good luck with your scholarship search!',
