        'description' => 'Are you currently (or will soon be) enrolled full-time in a university, automotive engineering program, trade school, or technical institute in the U.S. or Canada to pursue an automotive-themed major? If so, you may be eligible for the AmericanMuscle Automotive Scholarships! Twice a year, the scholarship awards $2,500 to one (1) current undergraduate student or college-bound high school senior who will be pursuing an automotive-themed major in their post-secondary education. In order to apply, interested students must submit a 700 - 1,500-word essay answering "who [they] are and how [they] plan on using [their] automotive education to incite positive change and innovation within the custom car industry." If you are currently or will soon be pursuing an automotive degree or certificate, we encoruage you to apply! Keep on reading to learn more. Bear in mind that this scholarship is offered twice a year, with deadlines falling on June 15th and October 15th of every year.',
