        'description' => 'Are you a registered Cherokee Nation citizen pursuing an Associate\'s, Bachelor\'s, Master\'s, or Doctorate degree? If so, the Cherokee Nation Higher Education Scholarships may be a great fit for you! The scholarship program is separated into three categories (Undergraduate, Graduate, and Stole Program), each with slightly different criteria. While undergraduate applicants may reside anywhere in the United States, those whose permanent address is outside the Cherokee Nation Reservation area or contiguous counties must be eligible for the federal Pell grant to be eligible for the Cherokee Nation Undergraduate scholarship. All graduate school applicants, however, must reside within the Cherokee Nation Reservation area or contiguous counties (see "Eligibility Information" for full list of eligible counties). Further, while undergraduate students must submit their FAFSA submission summary and recent transcript, graduate school applicants must submit a letter of acceptance to their graduate program and their most recent transcript to apply. If this sounds like a good opportunity for you, we encourage you to apply! Keep on reading to learn more.',
