[
        'name' => 'Jay Moum Memorial Scholarship This scholarship has been verified by the scholarship providing organization.',
        'description' => 'The Jay Moum Memorial Scholarship seeks to honor Jay Moum’s life by supporting graduating high school seniors planning to attend college and/or vocational school the following year. Qualified applicants will demonstrate a love for the game of golf, character excellence and academic performance. In 2025, two $2,500 scholarships will be awarded. The deadline for submission is June 20, 2025 and winners will be announced July 25, 2025. About Jay Moum Jay Moum was a great man with a big personality and a bigger heart. He grew up in Thief River Falls, Minnesota and lived to golf in the summer and hunt in the winter. He was tremendously talented at both disciplines and enjoyed those activities with his family. After high school, Jay attended Bimiji State College and played on the golf team while pursuing a degree in Education. He taught for several years before moving to Arizona and starting an amazing career in the road striping industry. By the end of career, he was respected and loved across the country. Along the way he raised and amazing son, John. He retired in 2014 to spend time with his friends and family traveling, connecting, and doing the things he loved. He started a second family and had a beautiful daughter Kia. He passed away too soon in May of 2020. Jay loved kids and was big on education! He helped many young people pursue ambitions by offering to buy sports equipment, pay for lessons and instruction, and for the creation of opportunities. He believed in young people’s potential and was always excited to watch them grow. Creating scholarship opportunities was always a dream of Jays. We hope to keep the dream alive perpetually.',
